You were warned to be careful around this fierce creature!  Maybe next time you will be able to elude the beast.	你已經被警告要小心這隻凶猛的生物了！也許下次你就能躲過那頭野獸。
Lucky for you that ogres are afraid of goats. This one decides to leave you alone.	算你走運，鬼怪害怕山羊。這隻鬼怪決定放你一馬。
You need to be a little closer to smell the flowers.	你得再靠近一點，才能聞到花香。
This is sad.  You are not the first to fail your quest in the Raging River... I hope you may be the last.	真令人難過。你不是第一個在洶湧河痛失冒險的人……但願你是最後一個。
This is the wild Raging River filled with boulders and rapids.	這是狂野的洶湧河，河中滿是巨石與湍流。
It would be dangerous to try and jump across the river on the boulders.	踩著巨石跳過這條河太危險了。
This mushroom is large and aromatic.	這朵蘑菇又大又香。
You reach down and pick a fat mushroom.	你彎下腰，摘了一朵肥美的蘑菇。
You see the familiar side of the Raging River.	你看見洶湧河你熟悉的這一岸。
The colorful mushroom is in the distance.	遠處有一朵色彩鮮豔的蘑菇。
You need to get closer to do that.	你得靠近一點才能這麼做。
The river is so swift it is a battle to fill the bucket.	河水湍急，想裝滿水桶得費一番力氣。
The water from this swift river is cold and sweet.	這條湍急河流的水，冰涼又甘甜。
You see King Edward's castle on the horizon.	你看見愛德華國王的城堡矗立在地平線上。
This lovely meadow is split by the Raging River.	這片美麗的草原被洶湧河一分為二。
There is no mushroom here.	這裡沒有蘑菇。
OUCH	哎呦
I can see you need a little practice climbing rope!	看來你爬繩索還需要多練習！
You should be more careful before trying that next time!	下次嘗試之前，你應該要更小心一點！
Your arms are like lead... from swimming.  You find it impossible... to swim any longer.  You sink to the bottom... of the well....	你的雙臂因游泳而變得沉重如鉛……你發現自己再也……游不動了。你沉入……井底……
The rope is out of reach.	繩索搆不著。
You cannot climb the sides of the well.  They are too steep and slippery.	你沒辦法爬上井壁，它們又陡又滑。
When you look upwards, you see the top of the well far, far above.	你抬頭望去，看見井口遠遠在你頭頂上方。
Although you can only see the bottom of the bucket, it looks like a very nice bucket.	雖然你只能看見水桶的底部，但看起來是個相當不錯的水桶。
How are you going to get the bucket?	你打算怎麼拿到那個水桶？
This is murky well water.	這是井裡的混濁井水。
The water does not taste as good as you expected.	這水的味道不如你預期的好。
In the midst of your activities, you fill the bucket with well water.	忙碌之中，你把水桶裝滿了井水。
The knot is tied very tightly.	這個結打得非常緊。
The rope is secured to the well with a very tight knot.	繩索用一個很緊的結固定在井邊。
The thick rope resists your efforts.	這條粗繩不為所動，你使不上力。
You have nothing to cut the rope with.	你沒有辦法割斷繩索。
Just before slitting the rope, you realize that it is not a very wise move at this time.	就在你要割斷繩索前，你意識到現在這麼做並不明智。
There is no reason to cut the rope.	沒有理由割斷這條繩索。
You reach up out of the well water and cut the thick rope that holds the bucket.	你從井水中伸出手，割斷了固定水桶的粗繩。
You have other things to think about right now.	你現在該想的是別的事。
A person in your position is in no position to raise or lower anything.	以你目前的處境，實在沒辦法拉起或放下任何東西。
I don't think that getting in the bucket right now will do you very much good.	我認為現在爬進水桶裡，對你不會有什麼好處。
You need to be closer to the water to drink.	你得再靠近水邊一點。
There is no way for you to get water now.	你現在沒辦法取水。
Now is not the time to try diving.	現在不是嘗試潛水的時候。
It is a very long, sturdy rope.	這是一條又長又堅固的繩索。
It is empty except for a huge boulder opposite the opening.	這裡是空的，只有洞口對面一塊巨大的岩石。
It is a rather large, vacant cave.	這是一個相當寬敞的空洞穴。
There is a large granite boulder and a magic mirror!! in the cave.	洞穴裡有一塊巨大的花崗岩，還有一面魔鏡！！
A green, scaly dragon breathing hot fire and smoke is protecting the mirror.	一條渾身綠鱗、噴著熾熱火焰與濃煙的巨龍，正在守護著這面魔鏡。
In this large cavern, there is a slimy dead dragon, an opening on one side, and a large boulder in the other.	在這個寬闊的洞穴裡，有一條渾身黏液的巨龍已經死去，一側有個洞口，另一側則有一塊大岩石。
There is no dragon here.	這裡沒有巨龍。
This ferocious, fire-breathing dragon with sharp, green scales and a long tail is protecting the magic mirror. Watch out for the flames!	這條凶猛的噴火巨龍渾身是鋒利的綠鱗，還有條長尾巴，正守護著魔鏡。小心牠的火焰！
You see the once powerful dragon lying lifeless before you.	你看見那條曾經威猛的巨龍，如今毫無生氣地倒在你面前。
A strange watery light issues from the hole.	一道奇異、如水波般的光芒從洞裡透出來。
This dragon had only one life and you have taken it.	這條巨龍只有一條命，而你已經取走了它。
With that dragon here?  No way!	那條巨龍還在這裡？想都別想！
This dragon does not respond to reason.	跟這條巨龍講道理是沒有用的。
You throw your bucket on the cavern floor.	你把水桶扔在洞穴地面上。
The dragon is protecting the magic mirror.	這條巨龍正在守護那面魔鏡。
The magic mirror is framed with ornate mahogany wood, polished to a high sheen.	魔鏡的邊框以華麗的桃花心木打造，拋光得閃閃發亮。
There is no mirror here.	這裡沒有鏡子。
Carefully, you pick up the magic mirror.	你小心翼翼地拾起魔鏡。
I do not think that you can get close enough to the magic mirror with the dragon here.	巨龍還在這裡，我想你沒辦法靠近魔鏡。
You could get a much better view if you were closer.	你要是再靠近一點，視野會清楚許多。
You are not close enough to reach it.	你離得不夠近，搆不到它。
You don't have any water.	你身上沒有水。
You have nothing with which to douse a dragon.	你沒有東西可以拿來澆熄巨龍的火焰。
You can't do that from here.!	你在這裡沒辦法這麼做！
The dagger sings through the air, but falls short of the dragon.  You should have been closer.	短刀劃破空氣飛出，卻沒能擊中巨龍。你應該再靠近一點才對。
You throw your water, but to no avail.  It lands on the floor and is quickly absorbed.	你把水潑了出去，卻毫無作用。水落在地上，很快就被吸乾了。
The water hits the dragon squarely in the mouth, extinguishing its roaring flames.  No fire!  How mortified and embarrassed the dragon is!  Moving a huge boulder in leaving, the dragon creeps off to sulk.	水正中巨龍的嘴巴，澆熄了牠猛烈的火焰。沒了火焰！巨龍又羞又惱！牠搬開一塊巨石，悻悻然地爬走生悶氣去了。
Nervously, you throw the dagger at the dragon and strike it in the heart.  Death for the dragon is instant.	你緊張地把短刀擲向巨龍，正中牠的心臟。巨龍當場斃命。
How do you wish to accomplish that?	你打算怎麼做到這件事？
You are too busy looking around to even think about that.	你正忙著四處張望，根本沒空想那件事。
You should know about these fire-breathing dragons!  Maybe next time you will be a little more careful!	你早該知道這些噴火巨龍的厲害！也許下次你會小心一點！
Your shield melted from the intensity of the dragon's flames!  You should know about these fire-breathing dragons!  Maybe next time you will be a little more careful!	你的盾牌被巨龍熾烈的火焰給熔化了！你早該知道這些噴火巨龍的厲害！也許下次你會小心一點！
I think you found the dragon!	看來你找到那條巨龍了！
Not even you can hold your breath forever.  The well bottom has become your eternal resting place.	再怎麼厲害的人也沒辦法永遠憋氣。井底如今成了你長眠之地。
It looks like this bottle has been here for a very long time.	這只瓶子看起來已經放在這裡很長一段時間了。
This is just an old, junky bottle.  You don't want it.	這只是個又舊又破爛的瓶子，你用不著。
It is very difficult to tell where the hole might lead.	很難看出這個洞通往哪裡。
The rusty old can has been here awhile.	這個生鏽的舊罐子已經放在這裡好一陣子了。
You have no use for this old can.	這個舊罐子對你沒什麼用處。
Thrashing around in the water has caused you to lose the magic ring and become visible again.	你在水中拚命掙扎，害你弄丟了魔戒，也讓你再次現形。
Even as you are reaching for your medevial flamethrower, the King's agents descend upon you.  You are taken away to be torched at dawn.	就在你伸手去拿中古世紀的噴火器時，國王的侍衛突然撲向你。你被帶走，將於黎明時被處以火刑。
King Edward the Benevolent is a very wise, but elderly monarch.  His frail body is almost lost in the large throne.	仁慈的愛德華國王睿智卻也年邁。他孱弱的身軀幾乎要淹沒在那張碩大的王座裡。
The King's throne is made of solid gold, accented with rubies.  It will be yours if you complete your quest.	國王的王座以純金打造，鑲著紅寶石。只要你完成任務，它終將屬於你。
When you bow to King Edward, his pleased smile warms you.	你向愛德華國王鞠躬，他滿意的笑容讓你心頭一暖。
The King, though very ill, seems happy to see you.	國王雖然病得很重，看見你似乎仍感到高興。
It is proper to stand directly in front of, and a few paces back from King Edward when addressing His Eminence.	與愛德華國王陛下說話時，理應站在他正前方，並保持幾步的距離。
You bow, but you are the only one who knows it.	你鞠了躬，但只有你自己知道這件事。
Go, Sir Graham!  Go and bring me back these treasures!	去吧，格拉漢爵士！去把這些寶物給我帶回來！
Welcome back from your quest, Sir Graham.	歡迎歸來，格拉漢爵士。
Why, Sir Graham, have you failed me and returned without accomplishing your task?  Go, and complete your quest!!	怎麼回事，格拉漢爵士？你辜負了我，任務未成就回來了？去吧，完成你的使命！！
Before exposing your flamethrower, you decide the King is just beyond the range of your obsolete flamethrower.	在亮出噴火器之前，你判斷國王正好在這具老舊噴火器的射程之外。
You are not close enough to see him clearly.	你離得不夠近，看不清楚他。
King Edward the Benevolent is sitting on the throne, waiting for you.	仁慈的愛德華國王坐在王座上，等著你。
It would show more respect if you were closer and in front of King Edward.	若你能靠近一點、站在愛德華國王面前，會顯得更有禮貌。
He bids you to approach so he can hear you.	他示意你靠近一點，好讓他聽得見你說話。
The King is walking towards you to commend you.	國王正朝你走來，準備嘉獎你。
Your heart also aches with pain as you watch the King.	看著國王的模樣，你的心也跟著揪痛起來。
The King is lying motionless on the ground.	國王一動也不動地躺在地上。
You are the only King here!	這裡只有你才是國王！
That's not a bad idea, but the custom in Daventry is to bow.	這主意倒也不差，不過戴凡確王國的習俗是鞠躬行禮。
To kill King Edward would mean immediate execution!	殺害愛德華國王等同於立即處決自己！
The throne is already occupied.	王座上已經有人了。
You will have to do that yourself.	這件事你得自己來。
This huge, tapestried room echoes every sound.	這間掛滿織錦的大廳，任何聲響都會迴盪不已。
You move aside as the King steps from his throne.	國王起身離開王座時，你讓到一旁。
As you approach the throne, the King himself rises to commend  you for a job well done.	你走近王座時，國王親自起身，嘉勉你這趟任務完成得漂亮。
"Oh!... Oh!!"  the King proclaims in pain!	「喔！……喔喔！！」國王痛苦地喊道！
From the seemingly lifeless King you hear these words:   "Well done, Sir Graham.  You have been a good and faithful servant.  Your reward is well deserved.  My kingdom is now yours."	你從看似已無生氣的國王口中，聽見這些話：「做得好，格拉漢爵士。你一直是個忠誠盡責的臣子，這份獎賞你當之無愧。我的王國，如今就是你的了。」
With those words, King Edward the Benevolent dies.	說完這番話，仁慈的愛德華國王便與世長辭。
The experiences of your quest will be invaluable to you as you begin your reign as King of Daventry!!	這趟冒險的經歷，將在你開始統治戴凡確王國、成為新王之際，成為你無價的養分！！
As you are leaving, your agents remind you that you must remain here now, where it is safe.	你正要離開時，侍衛提醒你，如今你必須留在這裡，這才是安全之處。
When you speak to King Edward,	當你和愛德華國王說話時，
he sighs and says,	他嘆了口氣，說道：
"Sir Graham, I am an old man. I fear	「格拉漢爵士，我已經年邁，恐怕
 my end is near.  I have chosen you to	 大限將近。我選中了你，要你
 prove yourself worthy of the throne.	 證明自己配得上這個王座。
As you know, our kingdom is weak and	你也知道，我們的王國積弱
 poor.  I have knowledge of the	 貧困。我得知
 existence of three things that would	 有三件寶物的存在，
 make our kingdom wealthy and strong.	 能讓我們的王國富強起來。
Somewhere within our kingdom, there is	我們王國境內的某處，藏著
 a magic mirror that tells the future.	 一面能預知未來的魔鏡。
 There is a magic shield that will	 還有一面能夠
 protect the bearer from mortal harm.	 保護持有者免於致命傷害的靈盾。
 Finally, there is a magic chest that	 最後，還有一個
 is always filled with gold coins.	 永遠裝滿金幣的金盒子。
Go, Sir Graham!  Go and bring me	去吧，格拉漢爵士！去把
 back these treasures.	 這些寶物給我帶回來。
If you succeed, you will inherit the	若你成功，你將繼承
